    "result_text": "The full build succeeds with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule following the app's existing Spring/MapStruct conventions for derived owner fields.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `namesakeCount`, `membershipNumber`, etc.), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipTier` backed by a `membershipTier(owner)` default method, mirroring how `membershipNumber`/`initials`/`householdId` are computed:\n   ```java\n   default String membershipTier(Owner owner) {\n       boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();\n       boolean noNamesakes = owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0;\n       return hasEmail && noNamesakes ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe `namesakeCount` was already populated at creation time by `OwnerRestControllerV1`, so the tier is derived from existing owner state. Returns `SILVER` only when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present; otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green.",
